; P5 (2026-10-25): float arithmetic joins as bit-exact integer work on the raw
; IEEE-754 words P4 made pushable -- no FPU, only shifts, compares and adds.
; f32.add and f32.sub decompose both words, order the magnitudes, align the
; smaller mantissa, add or subtract, renormalize through clz32; f32.mul runs a
; 24-clock shift-add on the 24-bit significands, in the shape of i32.mul. THE
; ROUNDING LAW OF THIS FLOOR IS TRUNCATION (round toward zero): every bit
; shifted out -- by alignment, by the carry fold, by the product fold -- is
; dropped, no guard, no sticky, no round-up. Overflow goes to infinity,
; underflow to zero or a denormal by the same truncation, x + (-x) is +0, NaN
; answers the canonical quiet word, and subtraction is literally addition of
; the sign-flipped second operand. Denormals are honored as inputs (effective
; exponent 1, no implicit bit) and as outputs. Division, fused ops, f64
; arithmetic and the f64 high half stay separate increments.
pub const OP_F32_ADD : u8 = 0x92;
pub const OP_F32_SUB : u8 = 0x93;
pub const OP_F32_MUL : u8 = 0x94;

